# Clean URLs — same set netlify.toml served. 200 = rewrite (URL stays clean in
# the address bar) rather than a visible redirect.
/menu           /pages/menu.html          200
/gallery        /pages/gallery.html       200
/about          /pages/about.html         200
/shop           /pages/shop.html          200
/careers        /pages/careers.html       200
/contact        /pages/contact.html       200
/reservations   /pages/reservations.html  200

# No /* -> /404.html rule needed here: Cloudflare serves a root 404.html for
# unmatched paths natively (not_found_handling in wrangler.jsonc below), and a
# catch-all rewrite would shadow every real asset path.

# Keep repo files that ship with the site but are not part of it out of public
# reach. Netlify's publish directory is the repo root and it has no equivalent of
# Cloudflare's .assetsignore, so the only way to hide these is to serve a 404.
# Verified exposed with a 200 before this rule: all seven docs/, README.md,
# MIGRATION.md, test.html and wrangler.jsonc. docs/INTEGRATIONS.md carries the
# Resy embed credentials and docs/QUESTIONS.md is open questions for the client,
# so neither belongs on the public site.
# (On Cloudflare these never deploy at all — see .assetsignore.)
/docs/*          /404.html  404
/README.md       /404.html  404
/MIGRATION.md    /404.html  404
/test.html       /404.html  404
/wrangler.jsonc  /404.html  404
